        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the woman whose appearance comes only from <Picture 2>, with her exact face, hair, eyes, skin tone and body from <Picture 2>; she is the only woman visible in every frame of the target video.\n<Subject 2> is the original woman shown in <Picture 1> and in <Video 1>; she is used only as a pose and motion donor and must never appear in the target video.\n<Video 1> is the source reel that donates camera movement, framing, timing, poses, gestures, clothing, accessories, environment and lighting. It does not donate any person's face, hair or identity.\n<Audio 1> is the synchronized audio track of <Video 1> and is reused as the complete soundtrack.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + reference generation + audio reuse] The target video is an edited version of <Video 1>. Every frame shows only <Subject 1> from <Picture 2> performing the poses and actions of <Subject 2>, while the original person from <Picture 1> and <Video 1> is completely replaced and never visible. <Audio 1> is reused as the full soundtrack.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - face, hair, eyes, skin and body identity from <Picture 2> are locked in every frame; no features of the person from <Picture 1> or <Video 1> are used.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): attribute_transfer - only pose, motion, gestures, expressions and body position transfer to <Subject 1>; face, hair and identity of <Subject 2> are discarded.\n<Video 1> (whole-video source): partially_preserved - camera, framing, timing, outfit, environment and lighting are kept; the original performer's face and identity are not kept.\n<Audio 1>: fully_copy - reused 1:1 as the complete final audio track.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic vertical 9:16 smartphone reel that strictly edits <Video 1>. The only woman on screen is <Subject 1> from <Picture 2>; the original person from <Picture 1> never appears.\n[Shot 1] Recreate <Video 1> shot-for-shot with identical camera, framing, timing, outfit, environment and lighting. <Subject 1>, with the exact face, hair and skin of <Picture 2>, occupies every position and performs every gesture of the original performer. No on-screen text, captions, watermarks, logos or subtitles.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe ambience from <Audio 1> continues throughout.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
        768,
        1344,
        124,
        "max"
      ]
    },
